.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr wg 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was written after 2026-08-17, when six Kubernetes nodes were Ready while
WireGuard had four peers: two control planes had joined the cluster and
never the mesh, and the host could not reach them on the addresses their
kubelets advertised.
It was found by eye.
.Pp
On 2026-09-29, writing this page: run as a user it asked the user's own,
empty, libvirt, so every machine read as absent, and it then reported
.Dq No drift: every subsystem agrees
over three sources that had not answered; and
.Fl -probe
with
.Fl -table
logged in to every machine and showed none of the answers.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
A row the database has and libvirt does not \(em
.Ql absent
in the table \(em is not a finding: Firecracker machines from
.Xr kfire 8
are recorded and live outside libvirt.
Check such rows by hand, and remove a dead one with
.Ql kldload-db vm-delete .
.Pp
It reports; it repairs nothing.
